[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114879,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "<p >Simple bone cyst (SBC) is an intraosseous cystic cavity lined by a fibrous membrane without epithelium, either empty or containing serosanguineous fluid.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:41:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114880,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114881,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FB80.5 Solitary bone cyst</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114882,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> solitary bone cyst.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> traumatic bone cyst; haemorrhagic bone cyst; unicameral bone cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114883,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "<p>None</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:41:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114884,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mandible is most frequently affected, with a predilection for the body {30792085}. Bilateral or multiple SBCs are fairly frequent {30792085; 9503460}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114885,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The vast majority of cases are asymptomatic and discovered on routine examination. Expansion is unusual and limited.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiographically, SBCs are well-delineated unilocular radiolucencies that scallop between the roots of associated vital teeth {9503460; 26850870}. A multilocular presentation is rare and typically only present in larger lesions. Cortical perforation, displacement of teeth, and root resorption are not observed, and expansion is rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114886,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SBCs are found predominantly in patients in their second or third decade of life, with no sex differences {30792085}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114887,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114888,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>More than half of SBCs in the peripheral skeleton have been shown to harbour either <em>FUS</em>::<em>NFATC2</em> or <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>NFATC2</em> fusion {32991339; 33316098}, one of the genetic changes seen in round cell sarcoma with <em>EWSR1</em>::non-ETS fusions {34081036}. Jaw SBCs have not yet been analysed.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114889,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sparse scrapings of fibrous tissue with bone fragments</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114890,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p >SBC has no epithelial lining, and samples contain nondescript thin strips of loosely collagenous or myxoid connective tissue with thin, lace-like fragments of immature bone at the periphery. Haemosiderin, cholesterol, and sparse osteoclasts may be present. Spiky, needle-like collagen fibres may lie peripherally and can become densely mineralized, a useful diagnostic feature when biopsy tissue is sparse {22034879}.</p>\r\n<p >Cystic haemorrhagic degeneration in florid cemento-osseous dysplasia has been termed &ldquo;SBC&rdquo; and may account for as many as one third of apparent jaw SBCs {17448841}, but the age group is older and shows a female predilection {21217632}, and these cysts are typically more expansile and may recur after treatment. Such cysts are probably not conventional SBC, but their mutation status is not defined.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:41:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114891,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:54:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
